Requirements: 21   with obligations: 20   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Requirement decomposition must preserve two distinctions when it reads a task
    file: an acceptance criterion demanding a test, against the behaviour that test is
    about; and a scope exclusion, against work the change must do. The constraints below
    state both.
    -> preserve-test-vs-behaviour-distinction  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the distinction between an acceptance criterion that demands a test and
       the behaviour that test is about, and preserve the distinction between a scope
       exclusion and the work the change must do.
    -> constraints-state-both  [functional/explicit]
       Treat the listed constraints as jointly stating both distinctions.

[constraint-01] An acceptance criterion that demands a test yields an obligation whose
    demand is the test, not the behaviour the test is about.
    -> test-demand-becomes-obligation-demand  [functional/explicit]
       An acceptance criterion that demands a test yields an obligation whose demand is
       the test rather than the behavior the test is about.

[constraint-02] An obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation demanding a test
    of that behaviour are never recognised as stating the same requirement.
    -> behavior-obligation-and-test-obligation-remain-distinct  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation demanding a test of that
       behaviour are recognized as distinct requirements.

[constraint-03] A sentence of a given shape yields the same kind of obligation
    regardless of which task file it appears in.
    -> same-shape-same-obligation-kind  [functional/explicit]
       A sentence with the same shape is classified into the same kind of obligation
       regardless of which task file contains it.

[constraint-04] Sibling bullets under one scope exclusions heading receive the same
    disposition as each other.
    -> sibling-scope-bullets-share-disposition  [invariant/explicit]
       Sibling bullets under one scope exclusions heading receive the same disposition
       as each other.

[constraint-05] A requirement disposed of without an obligation carries a reason that
    does not itself state a property the change must preserve.
    -> no-preserve-property-reason-for-no-obligation  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves completion-05)
       A requirement disposed of without an obligation has a reason that states no
       property the change must preserve.

[constraint-06] No obligation is produced whose only satisfying evidence would be a test
    that an excluded thing did not happen.
    -> no-excluded-thing-did-not-happen-only-evidence  [invariant/explicit]
       No obligation is produced whose only satisfying evidence would be a test that an
       excluded thing did not happen.

[constraint-07] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> byte-identical-inputs-byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-06)
       Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review state.

[constraint-08] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> tests-make-no-live-model-calls  [invariant/explicit]
       Tests issue no live model calls.

[exclusion-01] Whether an obligation needs test evidence at all, which is #148.
    -> preserve-test-evidence-scope-exclusion  [compatibility/explicit]
       Whether an obligation needs test evidence at all remains outside the scope of
       this change.

[exclusion-02] Assigning obligation types, which is #205.
    -> preserve-obligation-type-assignment-scope-exclusion  [compatibility/explicit]
       Assigning obligation types remains outside the scope of this change.

[exclusion-03] Which open questions are raised, and what they cite, which is #206.
    -> open-questions-and-citations  [human_review/explicit]
       Raise open questions when the task text is materially underspecified, and include
       what each question cites.

[exclusion-04] How finely a single requirement is split into obligations, which is #117.
    -> split-granularity  [functional/explicit]
       Preserve the intended granularity of decomposition by splitting a single
       requirement into obligations at the appropriate level of detail.

[exclusion-05] Whether obligation identifiers are stable across task-file edits, which
    is #231.
    -> stable-obligation-identifiers  [invariant/explicit]
       Keep obligation identifiers stable across edits to the task file.

[exclusion-06] Measuring how accurate decomposition is, which is #211.
    -> decomposition-accuracy  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Measure decomposition accuracy as part of the review process.

[completion-01] Implementation
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       A standalone section marker with no specific requirement imposes no checkable
       change.

[completion-02] A test asserts that an acceptance criterion demanding a test derives an
    obligation whose demand is the test.
    -> acceptance-criterion-test-yields-test-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       When an acceptance criterion demands a test, the derived obligation must demand
       the test itself.

[completion-03] A test asserts that an obligation demanding a behaviour and an
    obligation demanding a test of that behaviour are not recognised as stating the same
    requirement.
    -> behaviour-and-test-distinct-requirements  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation demanding a test of that
       behaviour must be recognized as distinct requirements.

[completion-04] A test asserts that sibling bullets worded alike under one scope
    exclusions heading receive the same disposition as each other.
    -> sibling-scope-exclusions-share-disposition  [functional/explicit]
       Sibling bullets worded alike under one scope exclusions heading receive the same
       disposition as each other.

[completion-05] A test asserts that a requirement disposed of without an obligation has
    a reason stating no property the change must preserve.
    -> no-preserve-property-reason-for-no-obligation  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-05)
       A requirement disposed of without an obligation has a reason that states no
